cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ISAAC in your work (the corpus, the pipeline, the models, or any
  of the access tools), please cite the paper listed under `preferred-citation`
  below. A single citation covers every surface of the project; please do not
  cite this repository separately. The `authors` field records who built this
  particular piece of software, which is a different question from what to cite.
title: "Illinois Social Attitudes Aggregate Corpus (ISAAC)"
abstract: >-
  Corpus construction, filtering, and labeling pipeline for ISAAC: a corpus of
  527 million English-language Reddit posts about six social group distinctions,
  annotated for moralization, sentiment, emotion, linguistic generalization, and
  estimated user location.
type: software
authors:
